{
  "results": [
    {
      "n": "G1",
      "evidence": "All five screenshots show the 3D French toast scene rendered cleanly in Chrome with no blank screen or errors.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "G2",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 2–5 show OrbitControls orbiting and zooming around the stack, and the code sets `maxPolarAngle = Math.PI * 0.465` and `maxDistance = 15.5`, though in screenshots 1, 2, 3, and 5 the grey cloth plane ends before the horizon, exposing the black background void.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "G3",
      "evidence": "After initial procedural texture generation, the runtime draw call count is modest (~50 meshes plus one InstancedMesh and one Points object), two shadow maps (2048 and 1024), and lightweight Bloom + Bokeh post-processing, which should maintain 30+ fps on integrated laptop graphics.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "1",
      "evidence": "All screenshots display a bottom UI bar (`#ui`) containing text ('Drag to orbit · Scroll to zoom') and interactive buttons ('Macro DoF: ON' and 'Hero Angle').",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "2",
      "evidence": "Inspecting the `animate()` loop in the HTML source shows only `controls.update()`, camera reset lerping, and DoF focus distance updates; there is no environmental animation running on load.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "3",
      "evidence": "Screenshot 1 matches the reference photo's close-up, slightly elevated three-quarter camera angle with the French toast stack centered on the dark plate.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "4",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–3 show three thick slices of French toast stacked on top of one another and rotated at slight offsets, matching the arrangement in the photo.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "5",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–4 show banana slices tucked between the toast layers, on top, and around the base on the plate, though several at the front base clip heavily into the bottom toast slice.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "6",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1 and 4 show blueberries clustered on top of the stack and scattered around the base on the dark plate.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "7",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1 and 5 show the stack resting on a dark round plate over a grey-taupe cloth surface.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "8",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1 and 4 show white specks scattered across the black plate and lightly over the top of the toast stack and berries.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "9",
      "evidence": "In screenshots 1–4, the toast slices have uniform, scalloped fluted edges resembling giant square biscuits or crackers rather than slices cut from a bread loaf with rounded crust and soft cut edges.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "10",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1 and 4 clearly show round banana discs with a faint three-pointed brownish seeded pattern in the center.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "11",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–4 show rounded blueberries of slightly varying sizes with distinct star-shaped calyx crowns on top.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "12",
      "evidence": "In screenshots 1 and 2, the toast slices, bananas, and berries interpenetrate heavily rather than resting cleanly on each other, and sugar specks float visibly in mid-air to the upper right of the top slice.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "13",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 2, 3, and 4 show closed geometry on the toast, plate, and cloth when orbited, though screenshot 5 reveals the back horizon edge of the finite 34×34 cloth plane against the black background.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "14",
      "evidence": "In the code (`keyLight.position.set(-5.2, 8.4, 5.4)`) and screenshot 1, the main key light comes from the front-left rather than behind-left, and the syrup drips look dark brown rather than catching bright warm highlights.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "15",
      "evidence": "Despite `BokehPass` being active in the code, `aperture: 0.00145` and `maxblur: 0.0065` produce almost no visible blur in screenshot 1; the back rim of the plate and background cloth remain nearly sharp.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "16",
      "evidence": "In screenshots 1 and 4, contact shadows around the blueberries, banana slices, and toast layers are weak or barely visible, leaving several berries looking ungrounded.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "17",
      "evidence": "In screenshot 1, there is a pure dark/black horizontal band across the very top of the frame beyond the cloth edge (`scene.background = new THREE.Color(0x161412)` unlit).",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "18",
      "evidence": "In screenshots 1 and 5, the syrup drips on the toast sides and puddles on the plate look like dark, semi-opaque brown plastic or chocolate rather than glossy, translucent amber with bright specular highlights.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "19",
      "evidence": "In screenshots 1–4, the toast has smooth, plastic-like gradients from pale yellow centers to uniform reddish-brown fluted edges, with no porous bread crumb or natural uneven pan caramelisation.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "20",
      "evidence": "In screenshots 1–4, the blueberries display a mottled dusty slate-blue bloom over darker skin with soft specular highlights.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "21",
      "evidence": "In screenshots 1 and 4, the banana slices look flat, pale grey-beige, and opaque, with dark grey/black shading artifacts around their rims rather than moist, slightly translucent fruit flesh.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "22",
      "evidence": "In screenshots 1–5, the dark plate shows a smooth ceramic sheen, but the tablecloth reads as a blurry, low-frequency mottled beige plane rather than clearly woven linen fabric.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "23",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1 and 5 show the plate and tablecloth sitting flat and level on the horizontal plane with no unintended tilt.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "24",
      "evidence": "In the code (`addCrustSyrupRivulets`), the syrup rivulets are static `TubeGeometry` meshes with no animation in `animate()`.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "25",
      "evidence": "Neither the screenshots nor the HTML source contain any steam or warm haze particle system or shader.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "26",
      "evidence": "There is no environmental motion in the `animate()` loop at all.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "27",
      "evidence": "In `createBlueberry` and `createBananaSlice`, each fruit mesh uses a per-instance seed for slight shape variation and distinct 3D rotations, though all blueberries share one `berryMat` texture and bananas share two textures.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "28",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1, 2, 3, and 4 show severe clipping: banana slices on top and at the front base cut straight into the toast geometry, and berries between layers intersect the toast crusts.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "29",
      "evidence": "In screenshots 1–4, the sugar on the plate consists of large, discrete, bright white polka-dot pellets (`IcosahedronGeometry`) rather than fine powdered dust.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "30",
      "evidence": "Screenshot 1 immediately reads as stylized/plastic 3D CGI—with cookie-shaped fluted toast, clipping grey-rimmed bananas, coarse white dots, and a UI bar—and could not pass for the reference photo.",
      "pass": false
    }
  ]
}
